      ]
    }),
    new TableRow({
      children: [
        tc("Projected Year-One ROI (Net)", { width: iw[0], bold: true, fill: BRAND_DARK, color: "FFFFFF", size: 22 }),
        redactCell(iw[1], 8)
      ]
    }),
  ]
}));

children.push(spacer(200));
children.push(p([
  new TextRun({ text: "The 90-day engagement installs the foundation. The $2,500 monthly partnership carries the work forward: ongoing strategy, marketing oversight, monthly check-ins, accountability, and the executional discipline that separates practices that capture the upside from practices that build the plan and never run it. ", size: 22 }),
  new TextRun({ text: "Luxora is built for 12-to-24-month partnerships, not 90-day vendors.", bold: true, size: 22 })
]));

children.push(new Paragraph({ children: [new PageBreak()] }));

// ============================================================
// SECTION 10 - RECOMMENDATIONS
// ============================================================
children.push(h1("10  Recommendations"));

children.push(h2("Strategic Priorities, in Order"));

children.push(h3("1. Seal the foundation before turning on ad spend"));
children.push(p([
  new TextRun({ text: "Every dollar spent on acquiring new patients before the internal leaks are fixed is a dollar spent at current blended LTV. The same dollar, spent after Phase 1, pulls a patient into a practice converting at materially higher LTV. Sequencing matters more than speed.", size: 22 })
]));

children.push(h3("2. Make longevity the growth engine, not the side business"));
children.push(p([
  new TextRun({ text: "The longevity vertical has 48% unbooked provider capacity, sits in the fastest-growing demand category in the trade area, and is the single strongest clinical differentiator against the competitive set. Treat it as the lead category in marketing, not the secondary one.", size: 22 })
]));

children.push(h3("3. Build toward an operating system, not a founder dependency"));
children.push(p([
  new TextRun({ text: "Every decision in Months 1 through 18 should be evaluated against one question: does this make the business more or less dependent on the owner. Scaling to location three is not possible until the answer is consistently 'less.'", size: 22 })
]));

children.push(h3("4. Preserve the premium moat"));
children.push(p([
  new TextRun({ text: "The competitive set is racing toward discounts. Long-term defensibility is built on the opposite stance: clinical depth, physician-led, results-defined. Every offer, every piece of creative, every script must reinforce that position. Never compete on price in a category where price competition commoditizes the brand.", size: 22 })
]));

children.push(spacer(300));
children.push(divider());
children.push(spacer(200));

children.push(p([
  new TextRun({ text: "Prepared by The Luxora Collective", bold: true, color: BRAND_DARK, size: 22 })
], { alignment: AlignmentType.CENTER }));
children.push(p([
  new TextRun({ text: "Premium revenue growth partner for independent med spas", color: BRAND_GRAY, size: 20, italics: true })
], { alignment: AlignmentType.CENTER }));
children.push(p([
  new TextRun({ text: "theluxoracollective.co", color: BRAND_GOLD, size: 20 })
], { alignment: AlignmentType.CENTER }));

// BUILD
const doc = new Document({
  creator: "The Luxora Collective",
